NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form supports arrays as values in a form, including sub-object values inside of an array."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To use an array, you can use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.state.value"},{"type":"text","value":" on an array value in conjunction\nwith "},{"type":"link","href":"https://svelte.dev/docs/svelte/each","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"each blocks"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script>\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      people: [],\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<form.Field name=\"people\" mode=\"array\">\n  {#snippet children(field)}\n    {#each field.state.value as person, i}\n      <!-- ... -->\n    {/each}\n  {/snippet}\n</form.Field>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This will regenerate the list every time you run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pushValue"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<button onclick={() => field.pushValue({ name: '', age: 0 })} type=\"button\">\n  Add person\n</button>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finally, you can use a subfield like so:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<form.Field name={`people[${i}].name`}>\n  {#snippet children(subField)}\n    <input\n      value={subField.state.value}\n      oninput={(e) => {\n        subField.handleChange(e.currentTarget.value)\n      }}\n    />\n  {/snippet}\n</form.Field>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"full-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      people: [] as Array<{ age: number; name: string }>,\n    },\n    onSubmit: ({ value }) => alert(JSON.stringify(value)),\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<form\n  id=\"form\"\n  onsubmit={(e) => {\n    e.preventDefault()\n    e.stopPropagation()\n    form.handleSubmit()\n  }}\n>\n  <form.Field name=\"people\" mode=\"array\">\n    {#snippet children(field)}\n      <div>\n        {#each field.state.value as person, i}\n          <form.Field name={`people[${i}].name`}>\n            {#snippet children(subField)}\n              <div>\n                <label>\n                  <div>Name for person {i}</div>\n                  <input\n                    value={person.name}\n                    oninput={(e: Event) => {\n                      const target = e.target as HTMLInputElement\n                      subField.handleChange(target.value)\n                    }}\n                  />\n                </label>\n              </div>\n            {/snippet}\n          </form.Field>\n        {/each}\n\n        <button\n          onclick={() => field.pushValue({ name: '', age: 0 })}\n          type=\"button\"\n        >\n          Add person\n        </button>\n      </div>\n    {/snippet}\n  </form.Field>\n\n  <button type=\"submit\"> Submit </button>\n</form>","lang":"svelte"}],"headings":[{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic Usage","level":2},{"id":"full-example","text":"Full Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Form supports arrays as values in a form, including sub-object values inside of an array.\n\n## Basic Usage\n\nTo use an array, you can use `field.state.value` on an array value in conjunction\nwith [`each blocks`](https://svelte.dev/docs/svelte/each):\n\n```svelte\n<script>\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      people: [],\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<form.Field name=\"people\" mode=\"array\">\n  {#snippet children(field)}\n    {#each field.state.value as person, i}\n      <!-- ... -->\n    {/each}\n  {/snippet}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nThis will regenerate the list every time you run `pushValue` on `field`:\n\n```svelte\n<button onclick={() => field.pushValue({ name: '', age: 0 })} type=\"button\">\n  Add person\n</button>\n```\n\nFinally, you can use a subfield like so:\n\n```svelte\n<form.Field name={`people[${i}].name`}>\n  {#snippet children(subField)}\n    <input\n      value={subField.state.value}\n      oninput={(e) => {\n        subField.handleChange(e.currentTarget.value)\n      }}\n    />\n  {/snippet}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\n## Full Example\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      people: [] as Array<{ age: number; name: string }>,\n    },\n    onSubmit: ({ value }) => alert(JSON.stringify(value)),\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<form\n  id=\"form\"\n  onsubmit={(e) => {\n    e.preventDefault()\n    e.stopPropagation()\n    form.handleSubmit()\n  }}\n>\n  <form.Field name=\"people\" mode=\"array\">\n    {#snippet children(field)}\n      <div>\n        {#each field.state.value as person, i}\n          <form.Field name={`people[${i}].name`}>\n            {#snippet children(subField)}\n              <div>\n                <label>\n                  <div>Name for person {i}</div>\n                  <input\n                    value={person.name}\n                    oninput={(e: Event) => {\n                      const target = e.target as HTMLInputElement\n                      subField.handleChange(target.value)\n                    }}\n                  />\n                </label>\n              </div>\n            {/snippet}\n          </form.Field>\n        {/each}\n\n        <button\n          onclick={() => field.pushValue({ name: '', age: 0 })}\n          type=\"button\"\n        >\n          Add person\n        </button>\n      </div>\n    {/snippet}\n  </form.Field>\n\n  <button type=\"submit\"> Submit </button>\n</form>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: arrays\ntitle: Arrays\n---\n\nTanStack Form supports arrays as values in a form, including sub-object values inside of an array.\n\n## Basic Usage\n\nTo use an array, you can use `field.state.value` on an array value in conjunction\nwith [`each blocks`](https://svelte.dev/docs/svelte/each):\n\n```svelte\n<script>\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      people: [],\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<form.Field name=\"people\" mode=\"array\">\n  {#snippet children(field)}\n    {#each field.state.value as person, i}\n      <!-- ... -->\n    {/each}\n  {/snippet}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nThis will regenerate the list every time you run `pushValue` on `field`:\n\n```svelte\n<button onclick={() => field.pushValue({ name: '', age: 0 })} type=\"button\">\n  Add person\n</button>\n```\n\nFinally, you can use a subfield like so:\n\n```svelte\n<form.Field name={`people[${i}].name`}>\n  {#snippet children(subField)}\n    <input\n      value={subField.state.value}\n      oninput={(e) => {\n        subField.handleChange(e.currentTarget.value)\n      }}\n    />\n  {/snippet}\n</form.Field>\n```\n\n## Full Example\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      people: [] as Array<{ age: number; name: string }>,\n    },\n    onSubmit: ({ value }) => alert(JSON.stringify(value)),\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<form\n  id=\"form\"\n  onsubmit={(e) => {\n    e.preventDefault()\n    e.stopPropagation()\n    form.handleSubmit()\n  }}\n>\n  <form.Field name=\"people\" mode=\"array\">\n    {#snippet children(field)}\n      <div>\n        {#each field.state.value as person, i}\n          <form.Field name={`people[${i}].name`}>\n            {#snippet children(subField)}\n              <div>\n                <label>\n                  <div>Name for person {i}</div>\n                  <input\n                    value={person.name}\n                    oninput={(e: Event) => {\n                      const target = e.target as HTMLInputElement\n                      subField.handleChange(target.value)\n                    }}\n                  />\n                </label>\n              </div>\n            {/snippet}\n          </form.Field>\n        {/each}\n\n        <button\n          onclick={() => field.pushValue({ name: '', age: 0 })}\n          type=\"button\"\n        >\n          Add person\n        </button>\n      </div>\n    {/snippet}\n  </form.Field>\n\n  <button type=\"submit\"> Submit </button>\n</form>\n```\n"}
